.TH EZYVIEW-MT5-BRIDGE 1 "2026-10-23" "EzyView 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezyview-mt5-bridge \- start the local MetaTrader 5 bridge used by EzyView
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezyview-mt5-bridge
[\fB\-\-check\fR | \fB\-\-token\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the local REST bridge on 127.0.0.1:8765. The bridge attaches to a running
MetaTrader 5 terminal through Windows Python and the official MetaTrader5
package inside the Wine prefix that runs the terminal.
.PP
On first use a random token is written to
.I ~/.config/ezyview/mt5-bridge.token
with mode 0600 and exported as
.BR EZYVIEW_MT5_TOKEN .
The app reads the same file, so the Bridge token field fills itself in. Without
a token the bridge refuses trade writes.
.PP
Wine and MetaTrader 5 are not bundled with EzyView. The launcher reports which
prerequisite is missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Request /health from a running bridge and print the JSON answer.
.TP
.B \-\-token
Print the per-install token, for pasting into Settings \-> MT5 setup.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EZYVIEW_MT5_BRIDGE_DIR
Directory containing bridge.py (default /usr/lib/EzyView/mt5-bridge).
.TP
.B EZYVIEW_MT5_PYTHON
Windows Python executable inside the prefix.
.TP
.B WINEPREFIX
Wine prefix that runs MetaTrader 5 (default ~/.mt5).
.TP
.B EZYVIEW_MT5_URL
Health-check base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:8765).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ezyview/mt5-bridge.token
Per-install shared token, mode 0600.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/EzyView/mt5-bridge/bridge.py
The bridge server.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ezy-view/mt5-bridge.md
Setup guide, including the Wine Python one-time steps.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ezyview (1)
